1
00:00:08,773 --> 00:00:11,973
You did say under the
chin, right, Polnareff?

2
00:00:12,233 --> 00:00:13,290
What the hell?!

3
00:00:13,373 --> 00:00:15,413
Remember me, you fool?

4
00:00:15,713 --> 00:00:17,913
I'm the Anubistan you fought earlier!

5
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:25,613
Matt, what do I do now? Goodbye!

6
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:28,092
I'm gonna shave your jaw clean off!

7
00:00:33,953 --> 00:00:35,659
Who the hell are you, really?

8
00:00:36,093 --> 00:00:38,387
And what have you done with the barber?

9
00:00:43,153 --> 00:00:45,113
Wait, could it possibly be that?

10
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:47,215
The sword is actually the stand?

11
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:49,392
Could it be controlling the barber?

12
00:00:49,793 --> 00:00:53,893
So the guy at Khan Ombo wasn't
a real stand user? Hold on!

13
00:00:58,993 --> 00:01:00,993
But in the end, it doesn't matter.

14
00:01:01,173 --> 00:01:03,526
I'm still way out of your league, buddy.

15
00:01:09,513 --> 00:01:10,343
What?

16
00:01:10,426 --> 00:01:12,213
How are you so strong?

17
00:01:12,553 --> 00:01:13,490
If you must know,

18
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:17,550
I took the liberty of learning
chariots' moves during our last fight.

19
00:01:17,633 --> 00:01:20,045
I won't lose twice to the same adversary.

20
00:01:20,393 --> 00:01:21,873
Do you understand me?

21
00:01:28,613 --> 00:01:29,443
To you,

22
00:01:58,373 --> 00:02:00,150
that's why I'm still looking for a goal.

23
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:05,113
I'm still looking for a
moment, when I'm in a battle.

24
00:02:08,453 --> 00:02:11,218
I'm going to fight against
the end of the game.

25
00:02:13,993 --> 00:02:20,653
I'm going to start a story,
and I'm going to die.

26
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:22,845
I'm going to keep going.

27
00:02:41,353 --> 00:02:43,110
HOLA HOLA HOLA HOLA

28
00:02:45,613 --> 00:02:46,470
HOLA HOLA HOLA

29
00:02:46,553 --> 00:02:52,693
HOLA HOLA HOLA HOLA

30
00:02:56,053 --> 00:02:56,883
You

31
00:02:57,233 --> 00:02:58,410
That's it you can do it.

32
00:02:58,493 --> 00:02:59,753
Yeah, come on.

33
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:01,010
You can't give up now.

34
00:03:01,093 --> 00:03:02,269
You've almost got it

35
00:03:13,753 --> 00:03:16,993
Polnareff and Jotaro they
should have returned by now

36
00:03:23,293 --> 00:03:24,690
Polareff, what's going on?

37
00:03:24,773 --> 00:03:26,302
The Barber's a stand user?

38
00:03:26,853 --> 00:03:28,153
Stay back, Jotaro!

39
00:03:29,353 --> 00:03:31,153
The sword is the stand!

40
00:03:32,193 --> 00:03:33,023
Trust me,

41
00:03:33,153 --> 00:03:37,310
it's too dangerous to try using Star
Platinum's bare fist against this blade!

42
00:03:37,393 --> 00:03:39,770
The sword's sharp enough
to slice through them!

43
00:03:39,853 --> 00:03:42,971
This Barber isn't the stand
user, he's just a puppet!

44
00:03:44,073 --> 00:03:46,132
And that's not even the worst part!

45
00:03:46,573 --> 00:03:49,220
The stand's even stronger
than it was before!

46
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:51,963
Bastard!

47
00:03:52,713 --> 00:03:53,543
Whoa, there!

48
00:03:58,593 --> 00:03:59,693
Too much for you?

49
00:04:01,793 --> 00:04:05,630
I suppose I should be grateful you've
shown me the limits of your defense.

50
00:04:05,713 --> 00:04:06,813
Most kind of you.

51
00:04:08,453 --> 00:04:12,688
Now then, let's see if you have what
it takes to survive my next attack.

52
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:15,373
Shall we, Polnareff?

53
00:04:20,973 --> 00:04:21,803
Polnareff!

54
00:04:26,613 --> 00:04:28,313
His powers keep increasing!

55
00:04:28,553 --> 00:04:29,733
With every strike!

56
00:04:30,113 --> 00:04:32,253
I can't keep parrying forever!

57
00:04:32,613 --> 00:04:34,613
Sooner or later he's gonna get me!

58
00:04:39,073 --> 00:04:39,903
Now!

59
00:04:41,173 --> 00:04:42,333
Take this!

60
00:04:44,773 --> 00:04:46,073
How in the...

61
00:04:47,793 --> 00:04:51,713
In case you haven't realized the
obvious, I know all your moves.

62
00:04:52,713 --> 00:04:55,093
It doesn't matter who my wielder is,

63
00:04:55,313 --> 00:04:58,313
as long as I've done battle
with you at least once.

64
00:05:05,173 --> 00:05:06,253
lose twice!

65
00:05:09,953 --> 00:05:12,393
I'm not gonna win this without my rapier.

66
00:05:13,153 --> 00:05:13,983
Oh, no!

67
00:05:14,373 --> 00:05:15,844
Jotaro, help me out here!

68
00:05:16,573 --> 00:05:17,653
Star Platinum.

69
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:29,790
Think that's finished
him off no that punch was

70
00:05:29,873 --> 00:05:33,313
shallow even though it took
just about everything I had

71
00:05:34,613 --> 00:05:36,453
Shit this guy's strong

72
00:05:37,153 --> 00:05:40,870
It's been quite a while now since
we've seen a stand like this one.

73
00:05:40,953 --> 00:05:42,653
It only relies on strength

74
00:05:45,433 --> 00:05:49,593
Not bad star platinum the
rumors of your speed were true

75
00:05:50,393 --> 00:05:55,053
But now that I've seen it
I can easily defeat it.

76
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:04,013
Hey, Khan, what's wrong
with you? Stay back!

77
00:06:04,273 --> 00:06:06,110
Your friend is being controlled.

78
00:06:06,193 --> 00:06:10,193
If you don't want to get sliced to
ribbons, go back inside and hide!

79
00:06:13,393 --> 00:06:15,217
We're in major trouble, Jotaro.

80
00:06:15,533 --> 00:06:18,553
The more we fight this
stand, the faster it gets.

81
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:24,274
And its next attack will probably
be its fastest and strongest yet.

82
00:06:24,493 --> 00:06:28,846
We have to be ready for whatever this
glorified butter knife throws at us.

83
00:06:32,373 --> 00:06:33,413
Move, Polareff.

84
00:06:33,633 --> 00:06:35,398
I'm the one it's really after.

85
00:06:35,613 --> 00:06:38,033
Get out of there, Jotaro! Die!

86
00:06:42,033 --> 00:06:42,863
What?

87
00:06:42,946 --> 00:06:44,053
With his bare hands?

88
00:06:49,433 --> 00:06:50,263
Amazing!

89
00:06:50,473 --> 00:06:52,649
For him to take that great of a risk!

90
00:06:53,733 --> 00:06:56,073
Now it's become abundantly clear.

91
00:06:56,433 --> 00:07:00,710
The true source of Star Platinum's
strength isn't its speed or precision.

92
00:07:00,793 --> 00:07:04,693
It's Jotaro's nerves of steel and
ability to make quick decisions.

93
00:07:05,813 --> 00:07:08,973
Yes, now I know it for sure.

94
00:07:20,513 --> 00:07:21,453
Is he dead?

95
00:07:23,473 --> 00:07:24,973
Hold on a second, Jotaro.

96
00:07:25,093 --> 00:07:26,387
He's just knocked out.

97
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:29,466
Whatever you do, don't touch that sword.

98
00:07:29,653 --> 00:07:33,690
You snapped it in half, but the stand's
powers might still be lingering.

99
00:07:33,773 --> 00:07:36,773
It controls anyone who
touches it while unsheathed.

100
00:07:37,033 --> 00:07:40,445
Let's get the blade back inside
without touching the hilt.

101
00:07:50,213 --> 00:07:51,093
Now what?

102
00:07:51,333 --> 00:07:53,530
If someone draws it again, we're done for.

103
00:07:53,613 --> 00:07:56,490
This damn thing has already
learned all of our abilities.

104
00:07:56,573 --> 00:07:59,455
I don't think we're gonna
get any second chances.

105
00:08:00,433 --> 00:08:04,090
Why not toss it into the river to
rust at the bottom of the Nile?

106
00:08:04,173 --> 00:08:05,233
The Nile, huh?

107
00:08:05,453 --> 00:08:07,470
That sounds like a great plan to me.

108
00:08:07,553 --> 00:08:08,383
Hold it!

109
00:08:08,466 --> 00:08:09,296
This is the police!

110
00:08:09,379 --> 00:08:10,570
This is perfect timing.

111
00:08:10,653 --> 00:08:11,890
This guy needs a hospital.

112
00:08:11,973 --> 00:08:14,590
I have multiple reports of
a brawl at a barber shop!

113
00:08:14,673 --> 00:08:16,732
What are you doing with that sword?

114
00:08:17,573 --> 00:08:19,430
Hand this weapon over immediately!

115
00:08:19,513 --> 00:08:20,925
Hey, stop it, would you?

116
00:08:21,353 --> 00:08:22,653
Don't pull it out!

117
00:08:33,873 --> 00:08:34,703
Polnareff!

118
00:08:36,053 --> 00:08:37,193
Oh, damn it.

119
00:08:39,113 --> 00:08:41,493
His eyes that stare.

120
00:08:43,413 --> 00:08:46,413
Polnareff is being controlled
by the sword's spell.

121
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:48,593
Hey! You there!

122
00:08:48,793 --> 00:08:49,933
You drew the sword!

123
00:08:51,973 --> 00:08:54,093
I drew the sword, did I?

124
00:08:55,233 --> 00:08:58,950
Officer, you should really be more
careful with your accusations,

125
00:08:59,033 --> 00:09:01,680
since you call yourself
a servant of the law.

126
00:09:01,973 --> 00:09:02,803
Take it easy!

127
00:09:03,013 --> 00:09:04,010
What are you doing?

128
00:09:04,093 --> 00:09:07,505
I'm simply attacking the culprit
who unsheathed the sword!

129
00:09:10,293 --> 00:09:13,110
I don't know who you are
or where you're hiding,

130
00:09:13,193 --> 00:09:16,781
but I think it's safe to say
Polnareff is under your control.

131
00:09:17,273 --> 00:09:21,391
Come to think of it, I've never had
to fight against Polnareff before.

132
00:09:22,413 --> 00:09:25,531
And I can't pull punches
with Chariot as an opponent.

133
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:30,813
If I'm not smart about this, I
could end up killing Polnareff.

134
00:09:33,473 --> 00:09:35,133
As I said before,

135
00:09:35,553 --> 00:09:40,050
at this point I've already witnessed Star
Platinum's entire repertoire of moves.

136
00:09:40,133 --> 00:09:46,613
And if I've done battle with you once
before, then I will never lose again!

137
00:09:53,153 --> 00:09:54,333
Okay, now.

138
00:10:02,693 --> 00:10:07,130
his speed it's incredible he's getting

139
00:10:07,213 --> 00:10:10,410
fast enough to outpace me i have to find a

140
00:10:10,493 --> 00:10:14,890
way to stop that sword i'll catch it again

141
00:10:14,973 --> 00:10:21,733
he's sped up this time i'll take your hand

142
00:10:33,073 --> 00:10:35,308
This speed and power are overwhelming.

143
00:10:36,313 --> 00:10:39,784
Without a doubt, this is the
fastest stand I've ever faced.

144
00:10:40,553 --> 00:10:43,082
At the rate I'm going,
this won't end well.

145
00:10:44,073 --> 00:10:48,413
I have to fight Polnareff with
everything I've got, or I'm dead.

146
00:10:52,753 --> 00:10:57,170
So, you headbutted the sword after you
realized you couldn't catch my blade.

147
00:10:57,253 --> 00:11:00,730
Honestly, I didn't think you were
capable of something like that.

148
00:11:00,813 --> 00:11:04,513
I almost had you, but now...

149
00:11:05,713 --> 00:11:08,073
I've acquired that skill as well.

150
00:11:10,833 --> 00:11:11,663
Jotaro.

151
00:11:12,513 --> 00:11:14,990
I can tell that you're
thinking the only way

152
00:11:15,073 --> 00:11:17,753
to survive is to kill
your friend Polnareff.

153
00:11:19,713 --> 00:11:23,301
Even if you wanted to, it's
naive to think it'd be that easy.

154
00:11:23,613 --> 00:11:25,553
Take a close look, Jotaro.

155
00:11:25,993 --> 00:11:29,993
What I'm about to show you will put
an end to this once and for all.

156
00:11:30,813 --> 00:11:37,153
So let's see if you can beat this, Dotoro!

157
00:11:38,013 --> 00:11:41,353
Feast your eyes on the
Silver Chariot and Anubis!

158
00:11:41,893 --> 00:11:43,069
Two-sword technique!

159
00:12:26,293 --> 00:12:27,173
Damn it.

160
00:12:27,653 --> 00:12:30,633
This extra sword, coupled
with this accelerating

161
00:12:31,653 --> 00:12:33,833
Even Star Platinum won't last long.

162
00:12:35,253 --> 00:12:36,312
What's the matter?

163
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:38,727
Are you feeling a little tired, Jotaro?

164
00:12:41,013 --> 00:12:42,954
I'll stop him before he kills me.

165
00:12:43,073 --> 00:12:44,033
Star Finger!

166
00:12:50,593 --> 00:12:53,213
My right arm is as light as a feather now.

167
00:12:54,593 --> 00:12:55,423
Interesting.

168
00:12:55,513 --> 00:12:57,101
I guess that was an option.

169
00:12:58,013 --> 00:12:59,730
Didn't see that coming, did you?

170
00:12:59,813 --> 00:13:02,053
Round two, armor release!

171
00:13:08,013 --> 00:13:09,093
You fool!

172
00:13:09,433 --> 00:13:11,750
Your ridiculous aura aura is no match for

173
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,653
two swords wielded by
two master sword men!

174
00:13:22,853 --> 00:13:24,953
Your stomach is wide open!

175
00:13:26,673 --> 00:13:28,373
I've got you now!

176
00:13:31,513 --> 00:13:33,393
I did it! I win!

177
00:13:33,933 --> 00:13:36,713
Master Dio, I've exterminated Jotaro!

178
00:13:37,193 --> 00:13:39,873
I, Anubis, have finally put him down!

179
00:13:40,613 --> 00:13:42,173
Victory is mine!

180
00:13:50,213 --> 00:13:51,553
Just forget it!

181
00:13:51,713 --> 00:13:54,130
You're not going to be able
to pull out that blade!

182
00:13:54,213 --> 00:13:55,154
Give up already!

183
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:59,850
I'm not sure your tiny brain has realized
it, But I've surpassed Star Platinum.

184
00:13:59,933 --> 00:14:01,713
And now, the final thrust.

185
00:14:04,053 --> 00:14:05,873
The final thrust?

186
00:14:06,213 --> 00:14:07,633
Yes, precisely!

187
00:14:08,153 --> 00:14:11,388
Once I slice open your bowels,
Master Dio will rejoice!

188
00:14:11,753 --> 00:14:13,113
Please, stop this.

189
00:14:13,293 --> 00:14:15,293
Don't drive the blade any further.

190
00:14:15,633 --> 00:14:16,463
It...

191
00:14:16,546 --> 00:14:17,376
it'll be murder.

192
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:18,653
Nice try!

193
00:14:18,953 --> 00:14:21,113
But you won't get any mercy from me!

194
00:14:21,313 --> 00:14:23,313
I can't wait to spill your guts!

195
00:14:28,113 --> 00:14:28,943
Hehehehehe!

196
00:14:37,733 --> 00:14:38,810
What the devil?!

197
00:14:38,893 --> 00:14:40,113
You're breaking me!

198
00:14:40,273 --> 00:14:41,633
I have to fall free!

199
00:14:42,613 --> 00:14:44,193
No! Stop!

200
00:14:47,593 --> 00:14:51,828
Maybe I'm wrong, but weren't you
saying something about slicing me open?

201
00:15:00,553 --> 00:15:06,013
I told you it'd be murder, but the murder
I was talking about was yours, friend.

202
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:10,539
You're a pretty easy target when
the sword isn't moving around.

203
00:15:14,213 --> 00:15:16,633
Damn it, what a pain in the ass.

204
00:15:17,153 --> 00:15:19,624
This was the toughest opponent I've faced.

205
00:15:19,953 --> 00:15:22,750
At last, the attack took everything
I had in me and then some.

206
00:15:22,833 --> 00:15:23,663
Luckily,

207
00:15:23,746 --> 00:15:25,250
it was just enough to
defeat him before he could

208
00:15:25,333 --> 00:15:27,980
learn it like he did
the rest of our attacks.

209
00:15:28,293 --> 00:15:29,333
This is new.

210
00:15:29,653 --> 00:15:31,453
I've never been so exhausted.

211
00:15:34,393 --> 00:15:37,433
I have to find Avdol and the old man.

212
00:15:42,433 --> 00:15:44,315
What in the world just happened?

213
00:15:48,133 --> 00:15:52,074
The sword didn't possess me like
it did all the other guys, did it?

214
00:15:52,213 --> 00:15:53,473
Yeah, it did.

215
00:15:53,753 --> 00:15:56,133
But it's over now. Forgive me.

216
00:15:57,593 --> 00:15:58,423
Just...

217
00:15:58,506 --> 00:16:00,093
get the old man and Avdol.

218
00:16:00,433 --> 00:16:01,873
I'm too tired to walk.

219
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:03,863
Huh?

220
00:16:06,313 --> 00:16:08,253
Wow, it's so shiny.

221
00:16:22,393 --> 00:16:24,913
Now, I've learned that trick.

222
00:16:25,213 --> 00:16:30,393
My original stand user was the
swordsmith who forged me 500 years ago.

223
00:16:30,813 --> 00:16:36,190
He may have perished centuries ago, but
I survive as a stand with no master.

224
00:16:36,273 --> 00:16:40,793
Master Tio liberated me from the
gloomy shadows of a dusty museum.

225
00:16:43,273 --> 00:16:49,373
And speaking of Master Tio, his stand,
the world, is far more powerful than I.

226
00:16:49,893 --> 00:16:52,713
That's why I pledged my undying loyalty.

227
00:16:53,253 --> 00:16:56,233
Jotaro, I swear on my life!

228
00:16:58,253 --> 00:17:01,113
I will murder you!

229
00:17:02,013 --> 00:17:04,513
I know your strength, your speed,

230
00:17:04,853 --> 00:17:08,030
you won't see it coming until
it's too late to stop it!

231
00:17:08,113 --> 00:17:09,953
I'll stab you in the back!

232
00:17:12,213 --> 00:17:13,333
Now die!

233
00:17:14,593 --> 00:17:15,423
You're done!

234
00:17:18,393 --> 00:17:19,713
What just happened?

235
00:17:20,813 --> 00:17:22,473
Son of a... I missed!

236
00:17:22,753 --> 00:17:24,293
I was tripped by a dog!

237
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:26,953
Where the hell did that butt come from?

238
00:17:27,533 --> 00:17:29,573
Hey, Iggy, what are you eating?

239
00:17:29,873 --> 00:17:30,853
Wait a second.

240
00:17:31,113 --> 00:17:32,853
Is that a nasty old sucker?

241
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:36,833
Eating right off the ground
again, you filthy mutt.

242
00:17:40,453 --> 00:17:41,873
You've gotta be kidding!

243
00:17:42,133 --> 00:17:43,313
It's the Nile River!

244
00:17:44,413 --> 00:17:46,393
No, this can't be happening!

245
00:17:46,853 --> 00:17:49,265
What did I do to deserve this cruel fate?

246
00:17:49,453 --> 00:17:53,113
If I fall into the river I'm
done for, I'll rust away!

247
00:17:53,793 --> 00:17:55,413
Somebody stop me!

248
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:00,833
I'm heading for a wall!

249
00:18:01,033 --> 00:18:02,373
The wall will stop me!

250
00:18:02,953 --> 00:18:03,913
Lucky me!

251
00:18:04,933 --> 00:18:06,753
What the? Shit!

252
00:18:07,113 --> 00:18:09,450
I was so panicked about
falling into the water

253
00:18:09,533 --> 00:18:12,290
that I accidentally face
right through the wall!

254
00:18:12,373 --> 00:18:13,653
I'm gonna fall in!

255
00:18:17,133 --> 00:18:19,373
Yes, it's a ship! I'm saved!

256
00:18:20,013 --> 00:18:24,170
If I wade into those planks, that guy's
curiosity will make him pull me out!

257
00:18:24,253 --> 00:18:26,993
